      en: "Maliele Art refers to the traditional rock art of the Basotho in the Maliele region, dating back to the 18th century. These artworks, found on overhanging rock faces, depict hunting scenes, animals, and abstract patterns, created using natural pigments like ochre and charcoal. The Maliele rock art is an important testament to pre-colonial Basotho culture and has been a protected heritage site since 1998. Archaeological investigations indicate the site was also used for ritual purposes.",
